module

public import WeilConjectures.AlgebraicGeometry.Modules.ZeroLocus
public import Sheaf.AlgebraicGeometry.TensorPullback

/-!
# Pullback compatibility of the zero locus

Source: `WeilConjectures/AlgebraicGeometry/Modules/ZeroLocus.lean`, theorem
`Hom.comap_zeroLocus`, lines 502-533 (blueprint: lem-pc-zero-scheme-pullback).

The pullback of modules is the recorded `Scheme.Modules.tensorPullback` of
`def-pc-module-pullback`, not Mathlib's abstract left adjoint `Scheme.Modules.pullback`
used by the source theorem; invertibility is `Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible` of
`def-sc-invertible-module`, not the source's `SheafOfModules.IsInvertible`.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory
open scoped AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

/-- The zero locus of a morphism of invertible modules commutes with pullback: the
pullback along `g` of the closed subscheme `φ.zeroLocus` is the zero locus of the pulled-back
morphism `(tensorPullback g).map φ`, as ideal-sheaf data on `Y`.

Source: `WeilConjectures/AlgebraicGeometry/Modules/ZeroLocus.lean`, `Hom.comap_zeroLocus`
(lines 502-533). (blueprint: lem-pc-zero-scheme-pullback).

Proof. (1) Fix `y : Y`. By `lem-pc-invertible-sheaf-instance` and
`lem-pc-invertible-common-free-generator` at `g y` there is an affine open `U ∋ g y` with free
generators `e_M`, `e_N` over `U`, and `φ e_M = b • e_N` for a unique `b : Γ(X, U)`. Choose an
affine open `V ∋ y` inside `g ⁻¹ᵁ U`; `lem-pc-zero-scheme-pullback-local-coefficient`
gives free generators of the pulled-back modules on `V` with coefficient `g.appLE U V b`.
(2) By `lem-pc-ideal-sheaf-comap-affine-extension` the ideal of `φ.zeroLocus.comap g` on `V`
is generated by the image under `g.appLE U V` of the ideal of `φ.zeroLocus` on `U`, which is
`Ideal.span {b}` by `lem-pc-zero-scheme-ideal-local`; so it is `Ideal.span {g.appLE U V b}`.
`lem-pc-zero-scheme-ideal-local` on `V`, applied to the generators of step 1, gives the same
ideal for the zero locus of the pulled-back morphism.
(3) The opens `V_y` cover `Y`; the ideal inclusions in both directions hold on every `V_y`, so
by affine-cover locality they hold globally, and antisymmetry gives equality. -/
theorem Hom.comap_zeroLocus_tensorPullback {X Y : Scheme.{u}} {M N : X.Modules}
    [M.IsInvertible] [N.IsInvertible] (g : Y ⟶ X) (φ : M ⟶ N) :
    φ.zeroLocus.comap g = ((tensorPullback g).map φ).zeroLocus := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules
